    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "There is a special equality involving an average:\n\n1/2(log x + log y)=log((x+y)/2).\n\nThe left side is log√(xy).",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So √(xy)=(x+y)/2.\nSquaring gives 4xy=(x+y)², hence (x−y)²=0.\n\nTherefore x=y.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_2": {
      "id": "q_2",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "content": {
        "text": "For positive x,y, if 1/2(log x + log y)=log((x+y)/2), what must be true?",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "input": {
        "type": "CHOICE",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "label": "xy = 1"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "label": "x = y"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "label": "x + y = 1"
          },
          {
            "id": "d",
            "label": "x = 2y"
          }
        ]
      },
      "questionReference": {
        "mode": "INLINE",
